## Context
The three documents came out of the design panel and read like it:
compressed, allusive, full of internal jargon ("corpus-critic M4", "graft",
"kill 9") that only makes sense with panel/cycle2/ open beside them. The
author's verdict (2026-08-27): "the house style is purely llm at the moment,
not my voice yet." Rewrite REQUIREMENTS.md, CONSTRAINTS.md and DESIGN.md so
that a newcomer — or the author in six months — can read each one top to
bottom on its own.

What plain means here:
- Short sentences, common words, every term of art defined where it first
  appears.
- The cycle-2 forensics (which critic killed what, the verdict on v1) leave
  the main line. DESIGN.md §1 compresses to a short "what changed since v1
  and why"; git and panel/cycle2/ keep the full record.
- Structure stays recognizable: R-numbers, C-numbers, D-numbers and section
  numbers survive, because tickets and DECISIONS.md point into them.
- Purify the requirements list (author, 2026-08-27): the list under
  "Requirements" holds R-items only. The D-entries mixed into it (D5 under
  Query, D6 under Corpus) move down to the resolved-decisions table, which
  already exists; where an R-item depends on one, it points to the D-number.
- Each document's italic front-matter preamble is replaced by a short plain
  "Intro" section: what this document is, who owns what, where the
  authorities are — in normal sentences, not a parenthetical block.

What must not change:
- Meaning. Every requirement, threshold, budget, decision rule and disclosed
  residue keeps its substance. This is a rewording, not a re-design; anything
  that reads like a new ruling goes through DECISIONS.md first, not here.
- The numbers: decimal comma, space thousands; the figure guard's anchors
  must be updated to the new sentences (the guard names every site).
- DECISIONS.md itself is out of scope — it is the append-only ledger, not
  prose to restyle.

If 0037's ratified amendments land first, they are rewritten here with the
rest; if this lands first, 0037 writes its amendments in the new voice.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] REQUIREMENTS.md, CONSTRAINTS.md and DESIGN.md read cleanly without
      panel/cycle2/ open
- [ ] The requirements list carries R-items only; D-entries live in the
      resolved-decisions table
- [ ] Every preamble replaced by an Intro section
- [ ] No requirement, threshold, budget or decision changed in substance
      (diff reviewed against DECISIONS.md)
- [ ] Figure-guard anchors follow the new wording; make check green
- [ ] The author reads all three and accepts the voice; any veto lands in
      DECISIONS.md first
